The first is "1+1i".
The second is "1+1i".
Keep a shared clean as empty text.
Keep a shared amount as 0.
The firstparts is split first by "+".
The secondparts is split second by "+".

To parse.
The size is the number of characters in clean.
The begin is 0.
The sign is 1.
The head is the slice of clean from 0 to 1.
If head matches "-", set begin to 1, set sign to -1.
Set amount to 0.
For every spot from begin to size minus 1.
The digit is the digit value of character spot of clean.
Set amount to amount times 10 plus sign times digit.

Set clean to empty text.
Place item 0 of firstparts into clean.
Parse.
The firstreal is amount.
Set clean to empty text.
Place item 1 of firstparts into clean.
The firstedge is the last position of clean.
Set clean to the slice of clean from 0 to firstedge.
Parse.
The firstimag is amount.
Set clean to empty text.
Place item 0 of secondparts into clean.
Parse.
The secondreal is amount.
Set clean to empty text.
Place item 1 of secondparts into clean.
The secondedge is the last position of clean.
Set clean to the slice of clean from 0 to secondedge.
Parse.
The secondimag is amount.

The realpart is firstreal times secondreal minus firstimag times secondimag.
The imagpart is firstreal times secondimag plus firstimag times secondreal.
The result is empty text.
Place format whole number realpart as text into result.
Place "+" into result.
Place format whole number imagpart as text into result.
Place "i" into result.
Show result.
